# Server (Hono + Bun)

The API is a Hono app on Bun. `createApp(opts?: { runner?: PipelineRunner; ai?: OpenRouterClient })` in `src/server/app.ts` is the factory — tests call it with `app.request()`. Inject a recording `runner` in tests; omit it to use `noopRunner`. Inject a stub `ai` for routes that call a model inline (`POST /api/documents/:id/draft-type`); omit it and those routes reject with "No AI client was provided to createApp" rather than reaching OpenRouter. Do not add Express or Fastify.

## Routes

- One module per resource under `src/server/routes/`. Register with `app.route("/api/...", routes)`.
- Register static path segments before parameterized ones (`GET /unread-count` before `POST /:id/read`) so the static name is not captured as an id.
- Parse JSON with Zod `safeParse`. Invalid body → `400` + `{ error: "..." }`. Do not hand a raw body to Mongo.
- Map driver docs through the shared schema before `c.json`.
- `app.notFound` stays JSON `404`. Do not leak stack traces to clients; log the cause server-side.
- A route that calls a model or reads a stored file inline returns the real underlying message (`502` for an upstream failure), never a generic "something went wrong". Log it too.

## Config

`src/server/config.ts` is the only module that reads `process.env`. Feature code imports `config`. New env vars: add to `config`, `.env.example`, and `keeping-docs-fresh` in the same change.

## Anti-patterns

Reading `process.env` in a route. A second HTTP framework. Side-effecting DB connects at import time in a way tests cannot isolate. Swallowing driver errors into a generic 200.
